course: dictionary
lesson: 6341
title: Context clues with mouser
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: You can often work out a new word from the words around it. These are its context, and they give you clues. «Real farm cats are useful mousers that keep mice and rats away from barns full of grain.»
explain: Mice, rats and barns full of grain are the clues. A mouser must be something that catches mice to keep them away from the grain. Swap your meaning into the sentence: "cats that catch mice are useful" still makes sense, so you have it.
explain: Words can also be used in a special way. Look for the capital letters in «Chief Mouser». That is a title, a special name for one particular cat, not just any cat that catches mice.
fact: A mouser is a cat, or sometimes another animal, that is good at catching mice.
fact: «Mouser» is a noun: one mouser, two or more mousers.
fact: «Chief Mouser» (UK) is the official cat at 10 Downing Street, the home of the British Prime Minister.
fact: Larry the cat has held the title of Chief Mouser at 10 Downing Street since 2011.
fact: In history, ships and bakeries kept mousers to keep mice away from food.
exercise: «Real farm cats are useful mousers that keep mice and rats away from barns full of grain.» What is a mouser? | A farmer who grows grain | A barn full of grain | A type of mouse | *An animal that is good at catching mice
exercise: Which words in «a good mouser» show what good means here? | *Skilled at catching mice | Very large | Cheap to buy | Kind to people
exercise: Larry is called «Chief Mouser». What is his job? | A dog that guards the door | *The official cat who catches mice at 10 Downing Street | A farm worker who grows grain | The Prime Minister himself
test: A mouser keeps a barn free of what? | Cats | Farmers | Barns | *Mice
test: Who is the Chief Mouser at 10 Downing Street? | A mouse | The Prime Minister | *Larry the cat | A farm dog
exam: Which of these is most likely to be a mouser? | A bird that sings at dawn | A fish that swims in a pond | *A cat that catches mice in a barn | A dog that fetches sticks
